{{!
    @template mod_playerwords/round_play

    Guess input for an active round. Letters, Backspace and Enter are captured at the
    document level by game.js's initPhysicalKeyboardCapture(), so physical typing works
    regardless of whether this input has DOM focus — it no longer relies on native text
    entry into the field itself. Submitting happens via Enter or the on-screen keyboard's
    own ENTER key, both routed through the same submitGuessForm() helper
    (form.requestSubmit()) — there is no separate submit button. The forfeit action
    lives in the page-level toolbar (mod_playerwords/toolbar), not here.

    The on-screen keyboard itself is a sibling in mod_playerwords/round_panel, not here,
    so it keeps sharing that template's own (tall) containing block for
    position: sticky — see round_panel's docblock for why. Since #playerwords-round-play
    is what game.js's showRoundResult() replaces wholesale when the round finishes, the
    keyboard living outside it means that function also removes the keyboard node
    explicitly, so it never lingers orphaned on the result screen.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "guesslabel": "Your guess",
        "guessplaceholder": "Type a word",
        "guessmaxlength": 7
    }
}}
<div id="playerwords-round-play">
    <form id="playerwords-guess-form" class="mod-playerwords-form">
        <label for="playerwords-guess" class="visually-hidden">{{guesslabel}}</label>
        <input
            type="text"
            id="playerwords-guess"
            name="guess"
            maxlength="{{guessmaxlength}}"
            class="form-control"
            placeholder="{{guessplaceholder}}"
            inputmode="none"
            autocomplete="off"
            required
        >
    </form>
</div>
